          "event_ids": [],
          "evidence_id": "sfev-85808e391cecf087",
          "evidence_type": "character_reaction",
          "paraphrase": "The narrator laments bearing the secret alone out of fear others would think him mad.",
          "provenance": [
            {
              "backend": "anthropic",
              "normalization_notes": [
                "used bounded whitespace/typography/case fallback"
              ],
              "raw_id": "ev18",
              "source": "model",
              "source_chunk_id": null
            }
          ],
          "quote": "Would to God I had let them share the search, that I might not have had to bear the secret alone so long; to bear it alone for fear the world would call me mad or go mad itself at the demon implications of the thing."
        },
        {
          "anchor": {
            "end_char": 40231,
            "paragraph_ids": [
              "p00065"
            ],
            "start_char": 40060
          },
          "confidence": 0.78,
          "entity_ids": [],
          "event_ids": [],
          "evidence_id": "sfev-86cd870b07742de0",
          "evidence_type": "inquiry_or_scientific_method",
          "paraphrase": "The narrator observes and analyzes the spatial arrangement of the mounds to deduce a pattern.",
          "provenance": [
            {
              "backend": "anthropic",
              "normalization_notes": [
                "used bounded whitespace/typography/case fallback"
              ],
              "raw_id": "ev09",
              "source": "model",
              "source_chunk_id": null
            }
          ],
          "quote": "Presently, as I gazed abstractedly at the moonlit panorama, my eye became attracted by something singular in the nature and arrangement of a certain topographical element."
        },
        {
          "anchor": {
            "end_char": 41011,
            "paragraph_ids": [
              "p00065"
            ],
            "start_char": 40815
          },
          "confidence": 0.78,
          "entity_ids": [],
          "event_ids": [],
          "evidence_id": "sfev-897fa9c21b7b6122",
          "evidence_type": "inquiry_or_scientific_method",
          "paraphrase": "The narrator deduces that the mounds radiate outward from the mansion as an underground tunnel network.",
          "provenance": [
            {
              "backend": "anthropic",
              "normalization_notes": [
                "used bounded whitespace/typography/case fallback"
              ],
              "raw_id": "ev10",
              "source": "model",
              "source_chunk_id": null
            }
          ],
          "quote": "That summit was undeniably a center from which the lines or rows of points radiated indefinitely and irregularly, as if the unwholesome Martense mansion had thrown out visible tentacles of terror."
        },
        {
          "anchor": {
            "end_char": 47114,
            "paragraph_ids": [
