          "evidence_id": "sfev-ea19207b32c600c4",
          "evidence_type": "inquiry_or_scientific_method",
          "paraphrase": "The investigators reason from conflicting accounts to form hypotheses about the creature's nature and mode of movement.",
          "provenance": [
            {
              "backend": "anthropic",
              "normalization_notes": [
                "used bounded whitespace/typography/case fallback"
              ],
              "raw_id": "ev02",
              "source": "model",
              "source_chunk_id": null
            }
          ],
          "quote": "We did, however, deem ourselves justified in assuming that it was a living organism highly susceptible to electrical storms; and although certain of the stories suggested wings, we believed that its aversion for open spaces made land locomotion a more probable theory."
        }
